rota lap 4414, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; read the concrete fact at the door ahead of the argument, so this lap ran each control's own sed against its source rather than reading REDS %519's sentence about the population
think Opened on fleet_round_open.sh at e80894d6fa; tree clean, no drain or gates sentinel; launched the cold roster pass with standing_equipment_run.sh --detach per the baton, which named its own transcript.
think Read the fourteen OPEN REDS rows and sorted them by whether a lap has a lawful closing move. %568, %626, %642 and %456 each defer to Keaton's word. %646's class had been counted by a peer twelve hours earlier (ff5e34b1f, gitlink_dependent), so taking it would have been %499 for the eighteenth time.
think Took %519, whose larger half the row itself names as a shape decision: 94 controls carry no plant check, and run_pen is written fresh in each.
think Measured first rather than repairing: tools/fixtures/p/plant.sh and plant_adoption_scan.sh already exist, adoption 20 of 214. So the cure is built and the open question is the other half -- whether any plant standing today is already dead.
think Read the four Caravan controls, my lane's own, expecting exposure. All four assert their plants through a grep -c on a needle the witness then reads -- a seventh local spelling %519's cmp -s census never counted. Not exposed.
think The sharpening that made the lap: a plant aimed at a file the control ITSELF wrote cannot go stale, since one hand authors line and pattern in one file. Only a plant aimed at a TRACKED source can be disarmed by an edit nobody connected to it. That bounds the population %519 could not name.
think Built the resolver twice over. First pass read 15 plants; widening the line selector to sed -i and line-start sed, then restricting to WRITING seds only (a sed -n ... p mutates nothing and counting it as an unresolved plant inflates the number with lines that were never plants), then widening variable resolution to prefixed assignments -- SCAN="$ROOT/tools/..." -- took the reading to 36 of 85.
obs Every resolvable plant in the tree is live today. The value is the wall, not the finding: the next type change that disarms a plant reds on the lap it lands rather than by the next hand who happens to look.
obs The gate has a closing move a lap may actually make -- aim the pattern at the line's new spelling or at its form -- which is what separates it from %626's gate over a number only testimony grows. A gate a lap cannot lower is a gate somebody turns off.
obs The witness graded C+ 77 on its first reading, register 48 at 52% negative sentences. Rewrote the header affirmatively holding every claim exactly: B 83. Reach 50 stays gate %7's open half, where module heads run 12-17 against Door's 9.
obs Against myself, twice. I opened the lap with an ls of the root the card forbids -- MAP.md is the walk. And I edited while my own cold pass was running, which is tree_moved, the fault PATCHOULI and COPAL each booked this week; the hot pass after git add is the green that ships.
